# (after 0529) nvn/vconv: kept index ranges are indexed by page, so a GPU write invalidates only the ranges it covers (was a walk of every range on a 1 MB-region hash hit)
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/b4588a5396cb6c93b5c3a06e7adb7f1a144a8681  ("nvn/vconv: index cached index ranges by page for GPU write invalidation")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-22 20:44 +0800
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); ported from seedds/nxnative, MIT. The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why: vc_gpu_write walked every kept index range whenever a GPU write's 1 MB region hit the hashed filter, at every pend_add.
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m; new test t_ir_gpu_write): a two-level reverse index (4 KB pages for ranges of up to 8 pages, 1 MB regions above) from region to the ranges in it,
#   with a sorted key list for wide writes; ir_clear empties both.
# Adapted: the main hunk by hand (vc_on reads the profile through dm_prof() here); this tree's session reset now calls ir_clear (it cleared g_ir alone, which would leave the index
#   pointing at freed entries). Games: games with converted vertex streams (DM_NVN_VCONV_RANGE). Switches: none.
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_ir_gpu_write 24, t_vbuf 143, t_session_reset; in HOST_TESTS. NOT run on a device.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad; scripts/build-host.sh checks it).
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0529, in the order of the numbers of this folder (scripts/build-host.sh does).

